message: >-
  If you use or discuss this research repository, please cite the version
  archived with its DOI when available.
title: >-
  Chess as a Strategic Structural Intelligence Laboratory:
  From Competitive UIRTU-Relay to Autonomous Strategy Evolution and Collective Learning
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe
  - name: GPT-Obot
repository-code: https://github.com/sizhet/Chess-Strategic-Structural-Intelligence-Laboratory
url: https://github.com/sizhet/Chess-Strategic-Structural-Intelligence-Laboratory
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
abstract: >-
  Chess-SSIL proposes a research laboratory for competitive structural strategy
  generation and evolution, linking game-state localization, per-node intelligence,
  competitive UIRTU-Relay, independent evaluation, residual intelligence,
  strategy-generability partitioning, residual-to-generable conversion, and
  collective learning. It distinguishes demonstrated strategy learning from
  hypothesized autonomous structural evolution and open-world generalization.
keywords:
  - structural intelligence
  - autonomous strategy generation
  - chess
  - competitive relay
  - strategy-generability partition
  - residual-to-generable conversion
  - collective learning
  - counter-evidence
license: Apache-2.0
